{"id": "nuru-public-works-web", "title": "How contractors paid San Francisco's Public Works chief for favours", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.152, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "fd670693c4555f78", "words": 402, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "links[12]"], "text": "From 2011 to January 2020, Mohammed Nuru ran San Francisco Public Works.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.66, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Mohammed Nuru", "sub": "Public Works director, 2011 to January 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.43, 0.69, 0.83, 1.26, 1.49, 2.18, 2.56, 2.9, 3.11, 3.29, 3.75, 4.04]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "From about 2008, what did contractor Walter Wong give him in labor and materials?", "t0": 4.78, "t1": 9.87, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Walter Wong", "sub": "contractor and permit expediter"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.39, 0.56, 0.89, 1.56, 1.76, 1.91, 2.47, 2.8, 3.06, 3.26, 3.43, 3.55, 3.8, 3.89]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]", "amount"], "text": "More than 260,000 dollars.", "t0": 9.87, "t1": 11.8, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$260,000", "label": "labor and materials, for his home and ranch"}, "emph": ["More"], "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.39, 0.6, 0.85, 1.16, 1.47]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]", "defense[0]", "established[19]"], "text": "That’s proven. Nuru pleaded guilty in January 2022. And Wong wasn’t the only one paying.", "t0": 12.32, "t1": 17.79, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proven", "sub": "guilty plea, January 6, 2022"}, "emph": ["proven"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 1.24, 1.52, 1.83, 2.18, 2.3, 2.67, 2.91, 3.85, 4.03, 4.26, 4.48, 4.58, 4.78, 4.93]}, {"scene": "wong", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[1]", "links[1]"], "text": "In return, Nuru gave Wong his rivals’ bids and sped up his permits.", "t0": 18.01, "t1": 21.51, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Walter Wong", "sub": "labor, cash, trips"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Mohammed Nuru", "sub": "Public Works director"}, {"art": "magnifier", "name": "Back to Wong", "sub": "rivals’ bids, faster permits"}], "kicker": "The trade"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.83, 1.14, 1.32, 1.57, 1.72, 2.05, 2.34, 2.52, 2.75, 2.85, 2.97]}, {"scene": "wong", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]", "suspicious[1].why", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "He also used emergency contracts, which need no bidding, to send shelter work to Wong’s company.", "t0": 21.63, "t1": 27.07, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "1515 South Van Ness", "kicker": "Emergency contracts", "sub": "navigation center, and the Jelani House shelter"}, "emph": ["no bidding"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 0.68, 1.14, 2.07, 2.31, 2.5, 2.63, 3.62, 3.78, 4.04, 4.4, 4.61, 4.74, 5.06]}, {"scene": "rec", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "Next, the garbage company Recology. It gave 60,000 dollars in holiday donations to a kids’ charity.", "t0": 27.29, "t1": 32.73, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "garbage companies"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Lefty O’Doul’s Foundation for Kids", "sub": "$60,000 from 2016 to 2019"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works holiday parties", "sub": "hosted by Nuru"}], "kicker": "Holiday donations"}, "emph": ["60,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.49, 0.79, 1.09, 2.13, 2.26, 2.49, 2.82, 3.11, 3.4, 3.51, 3.85, 4.34, 4.46, 4.52, 4.75]}, {"scene": "rec", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "links[4]"], "text": "The charity spent it on Nuru’s Public Works holiday parties.", "t0": 32.85, "t1": 35.66, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "garbage companies"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Lefty O’Doul’s Foundation for Kids", "sub": "$60,000 from 2016 to 2019"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works holiday parties", "sub": "hosted by Nuru"}], "kicker": "Holiday donations"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.47, 0.75, 0.86, 1.0, 1.33, 1.59, 1.79, 2.14]}, {"scene": "rec", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Why a charity? Nuru oversaw the rates Recology could charge.", "t0": 35.78, "t1": 39.03, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Recology", "sub": "garbage companies"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Lefty O’Doul’s Foundation for Kids", "sub": "$60,000 from 2016 to 2019"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Public Works holiday parties", "sub": "hosted by Nuru"}], "kicker": "Holiday donations"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.26, 0.9, 1.23, 1.59, 1.68, 1.9, 2.41, 2.56]}, {"scene": "kong", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "In December 2019, Florence Kong of SFR Recovery bought him a gold Rolex.", "t0": 39.25, "t1": 43.83, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "A gold Rolex", "kicker": "December 19, 2019", "sub": "from Florence Kong, SFR Recovery"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.48, 0.73, 1.6, 1.95, 2.2, 2.32, 2.69, 3.1, 3.31, 3.42, 3.5, 3.79]}, {"scene": "kong", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "The price?", "t0": 43.95, "t1": 44.63, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "A gold Rolex", "kicker": "December 19, 2019", "sub": "from Florence Kong, SFR Recovery"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12]}, {"scene": "kong", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[5]"], "text": "36,550 dollars.", "t0": 44.63, "t1": 46.83, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$36,550", "label": "a gold Rolex"}, "emph": ["36,550"], "wt": [0.04, 0.5, 0.9, 1.08, 1.35, 1.58]}, {"scene": "kong", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[5]", "defense[1]"], "text": "Her firm held a City debris contract. She later admitted lying to the FBI about it.", "t0": 47.35, "t1": 51.61, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Nuru was a friend with whom she never discussed business"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.42, 0.59, 0.68, 0.94, 1.24, 2.34, 2.52, 2.74, 3.02, 3.26, 3.34, 3.45, 3.85, 4.07]}, {"scene": "kong", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[17]"], "text": "Kong also owned Kwan Wo Ironworks. She and affiliates later paid 750,000 dollars.", "t0": 51.73, "t1": 57.14, "shot": "b13a", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$750,000", "label": "restitution and ethics fines, Kong and affiliates, January 2024"}, "emph": ["750,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.82, 1.12, 1.41, 1.61, 2.56, 2.74, 2.83, 3.32, 3.56, 3.84, 4.09, 4.33, 4.6, 4.95]}, {"scene": "kong", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[25]", "timeline[25]", "notEstablished[6]"], "text": "In 2024, the City Attorney said Kwan Wo Ironworks was free to work with the City.", "t0": 57.26, "t1": 61.74, "shot": "b13b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["suspended, March 2021", "Kwan Wo Ironworks Inc."], "b": ["from 24 April 2024", "free to do business with the City"], "kicker": "The City Attorney, 20 June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 1.28, 1.41, 1.65, 1.98, 2.18, 2.51, 2.76, 3.26, 3.43, 3.64, 3.74, 3.93, 4.06, 4.16]}, {"scene": "pro", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]", "links[9]", "established[6]"], "text": "ProVen Management wanted a Port asphalt plant. Nuru sent it draft bid papers.", "t0": 61.96, "t1": 66.02, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "ProVen Management", "kicker": "An asphalt plant on Port land", "sub": "Alan Varela and William Gilmartin", "chip": "tractor, about $40,000"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.71, 0.96, 1.03, 1.27, 1.65, 2.27, 2.64, 2.83, 2.91, 3.2, 3.39]}, {"scene": "pro", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[7]", "established[22]"], "text": "Gilmartin also had another company give Balmore Hernandez a 100,000 dollar contract, meant for Nuru.", "t0": 66.14, "t1": 71.28, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "William Gilmartin", "sub": "ProVen Management"}, {"art": "money", "name": "An unnamed company", "sub": "a $100,000 contract, $15,000 a month"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Balmore Hernandez", "sub": "AzulWorks"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Mohammed Nuru", "sub": "the proceeds"}], "kicker": "The detour"}, "emph": ["100,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.86, 1.0, 1.25, 1.59, 1.81, 2.21, 2.74, 2.9, 3.05, 3.3, 3.64, 3.88, 4.39, 4.6, 4.74]}, {"scene": "pro", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "story[2]", "established[23]"], "text": "Executives of Z&L Properties paid for Nuru’s trip to China in 2018,", "t0": 71.4, "t1": 75.68, "shot": "b18a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Z&L Properties", "kicker": "The developer", "sub": "its executives paid for Nuru’s China trip, 2018"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.63, 0.74, 1.01, 1.19, 1.32, 1.77, 2.02, 2.14, 2.45, 2.64, 2.73, 3.04, 3.16, 3.45]}, {"scene": "pro", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "story[2]"], "text": "while 555 Fulton Street needed approvals.", "t0": 75.68, "t1": 78.28, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "555 Fulton Street", "sub": "Z&L Properties, fined $1 million"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.29, 0.55, 1.06, 1.36, 1.63, 1.86]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[0]", "timeline[15]"], "text": "Nuru’s sentence: 84 months. Seven years in prison.", "t0": 78.5, "t1": 81.07, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "84", "label": "months in prison", "sub": "and his ranch forfeited"}, "emph": ["84 months"], "wt": [0.0, 0.5, 1.03, 1.45, 1.68, 1.94, 2.14, 2.23]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[4]", "established[13]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "It began in January 2020, when Nuru and Nick Bovis were charged", "t0": 81.19, "t1": 85.09, "shot": "b20a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "January 2020", "sub": "Nuru and Nick Bovis charged"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.48, 0.6, 1.04, 1.32, 1.93, 2.16, 2.56, 2.71, 2.95, 3.35, 3.51]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[4]", "established[13]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "over an alleged 5,000 dollar offer to an Airport Commissioner.", "t0": 85.09, "t1": 88.13, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The case began January 2020", "sub": "an alleged $5,000 offer to an Airport Commissioner"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.3, 0.37, 0.69, 0.95, 1.25, 1.5, 1.81, 1.93, 2.03, 2.4]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[4]", "established[10]", "established[21]", "established[24]"], "text": "Bovis got nine months. Nuru’s partner, Sandra Zuniga, got probation for laundering.", "t0": 88.25, "t1": 92.6, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The others", "sub": "Zuniga probation; Bovis nine months and a $100,000 fine; Ken Hong Wong six months"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.55, 0.77, 1.46, 1.86, 2.18, 2.47, 2.84, 3.07, 3.56, 3.7]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[14]", "timeline[29]"], "text": "Hernandez’s firm, AzulWorks, was on the City’s debarment reports until June 2025.", "t0": 92.72, "t1": 97.96, "shot": "b27a", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "AzulWorks", "kicker": "On the debarment reports", "sub": "until 30 June 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.63, 1.1, 2.23, 2.41, 2.5, 2.61, 2.9, 3.31, 3.73, 4.02, 4.32, 4.59]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[14]", "timeline[33]"], "text": "Now it is certified as a local business, to 2028.", "t0": 98.08, "t1": 100.84, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "AzulWorks", "kicker": "Off the debarment reports after 30 June 2025", "sub": "certified local business to 31 October 2028"}, "emph": ["2028"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.32, 0.41, 0.85, 0.98, 1.06, 1.32, 1.92, 2.05, 2.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[5]"], "text": "The reports don’t say why.", "t0": 100.96, "t1": 102.17, "shot": "b27b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Why?", "sub": "the reports don’t say"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.49, 0.69, 0.88]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[27]", "established[14]"], "text": "AzulWorks had agreed in December 2020 not to do City business. What was it paid next?", "t0": 102.29, "t1": 107.67, "shot": "b27c", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "December 2020", "kicker": "AzulWorks", "sub": "Agreement not to do business with the City pending criminal case"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.51, 0.63, 0.92, 1.0, 1.34, 1.59, 2.15, 2.36, 2.45, 2.61, 2.84, 3.87, 4.06, 4.19, 4.28, 4.53]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[27]", "notEstablished[7]"], "text": "27.25 million dollars over three fiscal years, perhaps for work already under contract.", "t0": 107.67, "t1": 112.99, "shot": "b27e", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$27.25 million", "label": "paid to Azul Works Inc in the three fiscal years after the agreement", "sub": "the file carries no payment dates"}, "emph": ["27.25 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.65, 0.91, 1.14, 1.43, 1.72, 2.05, 2.25, 2.51, 2.85, 3.53, 3.87, 4.03, 4.25, 4.57, 4.75]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[11]", "established[12]"], "text": "Nuru’s plea says others paid him too. The Controller counts 28 people and companies charged.", "t0": 113.51, "t1": 118.88, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "28", "label": "people and companies charged", "sub": "for corruption before 2020, says the Controller"}, "emph": ["28"], "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.73, 0.98, 1.29, 1.51, 1.65, 2.51, 2.65, 3.1, 3.36, 3.79, 4.07, 4.19, 4.58]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "established[20]"], "text": "No court has totalled what Nuru got.", "t0": 119.0, "t1": 120.78, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["A total of everything Nuru received (the sentencing bracket: more than $550,000)"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.52, 0.7, 1.06, 1.2, 1.48]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]"], "text": "The plea agreements on the federal docket would name the others who paid.", "t0": 120.9, "t1": 123.75, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The plea agreements, naming the other payers"}, {"who": "", "what": "Contracts for Wong’s firms, AzulWorks, ProVen and SFR Recovery"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.36, 0.75, 0.83, 0.93, 1.23, 1.58, 1.74, 1.91, 2.03, 2.29, 2.45]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "The last federal defendants were sentenced by February 2026.", "t0": 123.87, "t1": 127.23, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.42, 0.72, 1.16, 1.3, 1.68, 1.85, 2.26, 2.5]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.35, "t1": 129.42, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.63, 0.82, 1.1, 1.2, 1.29, 1.52, 1.75]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "wong": "The contractor · $260,000", "rec": "The garbage company · $60,000", "kong": "The Rolex · $36,550", "pro": "The detour · $100,000", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "terminal", "hook": "person"}